==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|ru|по́льза|-ный}}. The form of this adjective is the regular outcome of the Proto-Slavic stem {{m|sla-pro||*polьdzьn-}}; the first [[yer]] was strong due to the presence of another [[yer]] in the following syllable. The actual genitive plural {{m|ru|польз}} of {{m|ru|по́льза}} is phonologically unexpected, and was formed by analogy.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|поле́зный}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-полезный.ogg}}

===Adjective===
{{ru-adj|поле́зный|+}}

# [[useful]], [[helpful]], [[good]], [[beneficial]] {{gloss|having a practical or beneficial use}}
# [[wholesome]]
# [[usable]]

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-adj|поле́зный|a*}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ru|благотво́рный}}
* {{l|ru|приго́дный}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|поле́зно}}, {{l|ru|поле́зность}}

